      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-136147",
      ":question/problem": "The daily tide level in a coastal city, measured in meters, can be modeled by a function of the form $H(t) = A\\sin (Bt) + C$, where $A$, $B$, $C$ are constants and $t$ is the time (in hours) after midnight.\n\nIt is observed that at midnight, when the tide is rising, its level is exactly between the lowest and highest tides. The lowest possible tide level is $2m$, and the tide reaches its highest level of $8m$ at $3a.m$.\n\nWhich of the following could be the function $H(t)$?"
