      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-170535",
      ":question/problem": "A child is moving back and forth on a swing. The height of the swing from the ground, in centimeters, can be modeled by a function of the form $D(t) = A\\cos (Bt) + C$, where $A$, $B$, $C$ are constants, and $t$ is the time (in seconds). Assume that the positive direction is upward.\n\nIt is observed that when $t = 0$, the swing is at its maximum height, $65$ centimeters from the ground. Then, after $0.8$ seconds, the swing reaches its minimum height of $35$ centimeters from the ground.\n\nWhich of the following could be the function $D(t)$?"
